title: Gallax appointed Chancellor!
subtitle: The beginning of the end...
view-if: year >= 1933 and president = "DuFour" and (chancellor = "Goodryke" or chancellor = "Staal") and staal_chancellor_timer == 1 and in_grand_coalition = 0 and marcher_in_government = 0 and largest_party = "Royalist" and gallax_deported = 0 and not presidential_powers and not schleichers_scheme_success
on-departure: chancellor = "Gallax"; chancellor_party = "Royalist"; gallax_empire_end = 1
#tags: event
new-page: true

= Gallax Appointed Chancellor!

Internal scheming by the camarilla surrounding the president has caused President DuFour to appoint Gallax as chancellor, replacing the unpopular [+ chancellor +]. [? if gallax_deported : Despite his earlier deportation, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> leaders and their <span style="color: #3E88B3;">reactionary</span> allies have connived for the president to give him Commonwealth citizenship after all. ?] Some of the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span> surrounding DuFour believe that he will restore the Commonwealth to its supposed former glory, while others believe that they can control him and his movement.

He has promised a campaign of revenge against the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span>, and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> have already spilled blood. In his published manifesto, he promises a campaign of <span style="color: #7e0000;">**unspeakable**</span> <span style="color: #3f0000;">**horror**</span> against all who would stand for the republic, and endless wars to force the realms back under the Crown—a crusade that would set all of Athar ablaze.

What are we to do now?

- @fight: We will fight on the streets to prevent Gallax from taking power.
- @give_up: We will vote against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in the Assembly.


@fight

Do we realize that this means civil war, against the full force of the state?

- @civil_war: Yes.
- @give_up: We are not ready for war. Instead, we will vote against the Sovereigntists in the Assembly.

@give_up
on-arrival: in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; heartland_leader = "Goodryke"

Speeches are made. Votes are held. Bullets fly in the streets. Some <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span> are killed or jailed. Others flee the country. What can votes even do at this juncture?

The Assembly is burned, ostensibly by a foreign <span style="color: #700000;">collectivist</span>. In the wake, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> pass decrees giving them unlimited power. They, combined with the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if dnf_formed: <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>?], will win a majority at the next elections.

The Commonwealth is lost.

- @game_over
